config BR2_PACKAGE_POCKET_NATIVE
	bool "pocket-native"
	depends on BR2_PACKAGE_HOST_RUSTC_TARGET_ARCH_SUPPORTS
	select BR2_PACKAGE_HOST_RUSTC
	help
	  Nintendo 3DS games recompiled for the handheld, instead of emulated
	  while you play: a PC turns each game's code into a native program
	  ahead of time, and the handheld runs that plus the parts of an
	  emulator the game still needs — the system services, its GPU redone
	  in OpenGL ES, sound, and a frontend for a handheld with no desktop
	  (KMS for the screens, evdev for the buttons, ALSA for the sound).

	  A fork of Zakuro and 3dsrecomp by fearkov, which adds the OpenGL ES
	  renderer for Mali GPUs with no Vulkan driver and the handheld
	  frontend Banana needs. The games are not part of this or any image:
	  each player builds their own on a PC and copies it to the card.

	  https://github.com/whovian64/pocket-native

comment "pocket-native needs a toolchain with Rust"
	depends on !BR2_PACKAGE_HOST_RUSTC_TARGET_ARCH_SUPPORTS
